.SH NAME
niac-mibzip-inspect - Inspect a file for MibZip format


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBniac mibzip inspect  [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspect a file and report whether it uses NIAC MibZip format.

.PP
For MibZip files, the command also reports the number of expanded walk entries
so operators can quickly verify the compressed asset is readable.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for inspect


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--storage-keep\fP=500
	Run history records to keep, pruned oldest first on start (0 keeps every run)

.PP
\fB--storage-path\fP=""
	Path to NIAC run history database (default: ~/.niac/niac.db)


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  niac mibzip inspect walks/cisco-c9300.mz
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBniac-mibzip(1)\fP


